 "editsOutsideTheBatchFiles": [
  "concepts.json: the concept potato also lists minecraft:potatoes (the planted crop block), so a step may teach 감자 on a PLACE_REL of the crop.",
  "concepts.json: descKo for gen_pumpkin_pie (호박 파이) and gen_mushroom_stew (버섯 스튜), which the batch teaches.",
  "src/test/resources/content-baseline.json: baeckerei and teppichpfad removed from reachabilityDebt (they no longer ask for Nether or End things).",
  "docs/book/src/quest-tree.md and chapters.json regenerated; content/korean/lines.jsonl and review-status.json regenerated."
 ],
 "generatorWeaknesses": [
  "No verb for 요리하다 or 수영하다 (quest/Verb.java): SMELT of food reads 구워요, IN_WATER only prefixes 물속에서. Both verbs are authored, and an authored clue must (a) have no condition, (b) contain the first taught word as a dictionary substring and (c) name the goal's action verb (QuestlineValidationTest), so a verb word can never be the first taught word and 수영해요 cannot sit on an IN_WATER step. The two clues are two-sentence lines: \"닭을 요리해요. 맛있게 만들어요.\" (SMELT) and \"바다로 가요. 수영해요.\" (REACH_BIOME).",
  "Authored clues are thrown away for any step that has a condition (QuestTextService.clueKo), so flavour sentences (비가 내려요, 해가 떠요) only work on condition-free steps.",
  "REACH_BIOME and a biome condition always say the first taught word instead of the biome name (SentenceBuilder.objectName): a step that teaches 개구리 reads \"개구리로 가요\" for a swamp. The teach list has to start with the biome concept.",
  "Fluids cannot be an anchor: PLACE_REL on minecraft:water fails (\"has no Korean name\") and LOOK_AT_BLOCK cannot target water, so no \"물 위에 수련잎을 놓아요\".",
  "PLAYER_REL accepts no tag as anchor (\"#minecraft:logs\" reads 그것), PLACE_REL does.",
  "BUILD_PATTERN RING speaks 울타리, so a ring of planks is \"판자로 울타리를 쌓아요\" and a ring of fences is \"울타리로 울타리를\"; the ring of the island is sand.",
  "The ceremony (finale) line speaks registry names: 참나무 울타리 기둥 위에 양털을 놓았어요, 눈 블록 기둥 위에, 하얀색 양탄자 위에서; only generated finales are possible (SentenceDumpTest wants more than 300).",
  "The Namer shortens 눈 블록 to 눈 in clues (\"눈을 두 개 만들어요\"), which can read as \"two eyes\" without the snowball step before it.",
  "REACH_HEIGHT teaching 올라가다: the clue never contains the dictionary form, so the first taught word must be 산 (minY 100 reads \"산 위로\"; below 100 it reads 언덕 and no concept matches). 들어가다 (cave biomes) has no gentle name: dripstone caves read 점적석 동굴.",
  "Every unknown-words slot is spent by a new word: a new word needs three earlier steps before it is known, so a sentence with two new words (for example a new ingredient and a new dish) breaks coverage.sentences.unknownOverOneShare. The batch therefore introduces one new word per sentence and lets the ingredient lists of CRAFT (`with`) go.",
  "Multi-word teach lists need an authored hint that contains every noun (WaveQaTest), so the batch teaches one word per step except where the hint is authored."
 ]
}
